# Frontend file placement

Put new files in a domain folder. Do not add to `src/pages/`, `src/components/`, or `src/lib/` roots.

| Kind | Put it here |
|------|-------------|
| Route page | `src/pages/<domain>/` (`sales`, `finance`, `operations`, `hr`, `office`, `workspace`, `system`, …) |
| UI for a desk | `src/components/<domain>/` |
| Shell / chrome | `src/components/layout/` |
| Auth, login, route guards | `src/components/auth/` |
| Browser-only helpers | `src/lib/<domain>/` or `src/lib/<topic>.js` |
| Logic shared with the API | `src/shared/` (copy from backend `shared/` via `npm run sync:shared`) |

Do not duplicate backend `shared/lib` into `src/lib`. Extend `scripts/sync-shared-from-backend.mjs` and import from `src/shared/`.

When moving a file, update every import and `vite.config.js` `manualChunks` paths in the same change. Do not leave compatibility stubs unless a public import must stay stable.

Do not move files that already have unrelated uncommitted edits.
